**Open question for Taha:** swipe-left is currently *skip* (advance) with no persisted "dislike" — nothing consumes a dislike (no ranking/counts, #4). Say the word to add one.

**Accessibility floor (non-negotiable, holds despite the principle 5/6 reversal):** every gesture action also has a labelled button *and* a keyboard shortcut *and* an aria-live announcement; the persistent media-transport `RadioPlayer` stays mounted; press-and-hold always has a tap twin. Screen readers consume raw swipes, so these non-gesture routes are what actually reach a blind user. The reversal + its unresolved engineering dissent are recorded publicly in spec **§4.1**.

**Still unverified (do NOT claim):** no screen-reader user has driven the deck on a real device. The "gestures are more accessible for blind people" rationale is a leadership view, not a measured result.

